  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Extends the integrated general Buchmann--Lenstra cycle with an exact proven-prime p-radical path, using the tame trace radical for p greater than the degree and a sufficiently high Frobenius kernel for wild small primes. A stable buchmann_lenstra_multiplier_cycle API canonicalizes arbitrary current OrderBasis inputs, reuses the existing certified multiplier/HNF/event machinery, and certifies prime fixed points. Sage 10.9 fixtures cover the two irregular polygon timeout cases; the crossover benchmark shows one saved radical iteration and 1.60x--1.89x measured speedup when reusing polygon/current-order evidence. The final portable follow-up removes a prose-only runtime namespace false positive in local_polygons.py.",
    "risks": [
      "Focused CPython/Sage.js differential tests, strict Pyright/Ruff, the benchmark guard, and an ad hoc Sage 10.9 comparison across 30 local primes in 24 deterministic irreducible cubics pass."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Cherry-pick this lane and route proven-prime nonidentity/current-order local fallbacks to buchmann_lenstra_multiplier_cycle.",
      "Retain the selector's preference for polygon-produced current-order evidence on the two irregular cubic families."
    ]
  }
